059, 0.012668424, -0.023603326, -0.043366272, 0.04254779, -0.055509456, -0.022404071, -0.0045852684, -0.02821963, -0.039412815, 0.04545889, -0.05260589, 0.033785213, 0.001020621, -0.019146517, 0.012960722, -0.07874475, 0.014017476, 0.0066331676, -0.023633003, 0.13098711, -0.010303007, -0.0077040694, 0.029689813, 0.0016462418, -0.16031393, -0.005197547, -0.001397436, 0.019433541, -0.030353477, 0.06437262, -0.0389516, -0.020218201, 0.055976924, -0.032659754, 0.019072918, 0.003336723, -0.03307317, -0.03616326, 0.011863001, 0.04195034, -0.022632793, 0.03142315, -0.0036088699, -0.106744334, 0.034792133, -0.019564781, 0.106966384, 0.0055690478, 0.03738782, -0.010580333, 0.0011601839, -0.04541622, -0.051602904, 0.011259001, 0.053305686, -0.03952725, 0.017852783, 0.0042134263, 0.015896732, 0.053370874, 0.14177328, -0.007778325, 0.053306114, -0.047162592, 0.12300651, 0.0036051797, 0.0034268142, -0.041530304, 0.09346375, 0.03672333, -0.015392398, 0.024547612, -0.040519852, -0.021072779, -0.019277219, -0.04298978, -0.07471046, -0.047274187, -0.007472773, 0.042631622, 0.0062389583, -0.031515636, 0.015586583, -0.026336044, -0.03160406, 0.03945434, -0.00837255, -0.105692826, -0.004510566], embedding_model: 'snowflake-arctic-embed-xs@d8c86521', source: source:`isu_apple_scab`, text: 'Cultural methods of disease management produce better results in relatively dry years and, in some situations, may even eliminate the need for fungicides. A properly pruned open tree canopy has better ventilation which allows for faster drying of leaves, reducing the number of infections. Because the apple scab fungus overwinters in leaf litter, sanitation is the primary measure to manage scab.\nSatiation means removing fallen leaves where the fungus will overwinter. In the autumn, removing and destroying fallen foliage (chopped and composted to proper temperatures or discarded as trash) will dramatically reduce the number of this pathogen available to infect trees next year. The best line of defense against this disease would be to plant scab-resistant cultivars and prune and training trees to allow good air circulation.\nThere are fungicides labeled for the control of apple scab. Spraying scab-susceptible trees with preventive treatment (before the symptoms are observed) may help reduce this disease, but scab is usually not a deadly disease.', text_hash: 'd410695b5a9cb469c81fbb04774bbddde10d343bc59a14d91f07091665ecdc35', topic: 'management' } RETURN NONE;
