 -0.07548659, 0.031682555, 0.008163729, -0.06094341, -0.06669938, -0.028690984, -0.0033454983, -0.021951642, -0.010096931, 0.044326246, 0.03673877, -0.025318952, -0.004099555, -0.09009017, 0.05341137, 0.019555353, -0.0096162595, 0.08376753, -0.031974383, 0.052891172, 0.0029161512, 0.010833317, -0.15468703, -0.041753236, 0.015126902, 0.011303828, -0.02156113, 0.03211965, 0.006397039, 0.041029893, 0.013656723, 0.004985049, 0.10212936, 0.035177033, -0.008738495, -0.048161604, -0.010478171, 0.078793466, -0.073723786, -0.015036969, 0.02527986, -0.10702617, 0.04169239, -0.0011310527, 0.06955619, -0.0024970516, 0.08323002, 0.015361946, 0.013689471, -0.11993658, -0.06842414, 0.01623991, -0.01923427, -0.015822181, -0.053188864, 0.0043216967, -0.02094536, 0.011567901, 0.0863801, -0.0040092464, -0.0033694913, -0.065872684, 0.16970623, -0.0291961, -0.020793986, -0.023858288, 0.049669992, -0.04190684, -0.017476369, -0.025366476, 0.019696662, -0.021113565, -0.0076634604, -0.00010580911, -0.015960414, 0.03943902, 0.027185226, 0.037384436, 0.052399132, 0.03100478, 0.036671296, -0.038811117, -0.021756226, -0.029359393, 0.027987646, -0.08058983, -0.02028316], embedding_model: 'snowflake-arctic-embed-xs@d8c86521', source: source:`ontario_field_crops_soil_management`, text: 'Over time, the approach to soil management has an influence on the health of the soil. Assessing the soil health for each field, and taking steps to maintain or improve it, will help ensure high productivity. Maintaining soil health is a long-term process.\nSome management practices will improve the soil and others will degrade it. The changes can occur relatively slowly, or quickly. How will the impact of past and current management practices on the soil be determined? Some measures are easy and relatively inexpensive to implement, while others require more effort and commitment. The following are a number of soil characteristics and simple assessments that can determine the status of each.', text_hash: '7d87a2810